{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FvhCB93jqt4LU48te2ZGuN","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report with all the key details.\n\n## Complete Implementation Report: Zerocheck and Logup Monomial Kernels\n\nBased on thorough analysis of the CUDA backend and Rust FFI bindings, here's the complete structure of the zerocheck and logup monomial kernel implementation:\n\n---\n\n### **1. CUDA KERNEL FILE: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`**\n\n#### **Key Data Structures (Lines 46-54, 368-381, 393-398)**\n\n```cuda\n// MonomialAirCtx struct (per-AIR context)\nstruct MonomialAirCtx {\n    const MonomialHeader *__restrict__ d_headers;\n    const PackedVar *__restrict__ d_variables;\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_lambda_combinations; // Precomputed per-monomial\n    uint32_t num_monomials;\n    EvalCoreCtx eval_ctx;\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_eq_xi;\n    uint32_t num_y;\n};\n\n// LogupMonomialCommonCtx - shared per-AIR context for logup (line 368-374)\nstruct LogupMonomialCommonCtx {\n    EvalCoreCtx eval_ctx;\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_eq_xi;\n    FpExt bus_term_sum; // Precomputed sum_i(beta[message_len_i] * (bus_idx[i]+1) * eq_3bs[i])\n    uint32_t num_y;\n    uint32_t mono_blocks;\n};\n\n// LogupMonomialCtx - per-monomial type (numerator or denominator)\nstruct LogupMonomialCtx {\n    const MonomialHeader *__restrict__ d_headers;\n    const PackedVar *__restrict__ d_variables;\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_combinations;\n    uint32_t num_monomials;\n};\n```\n\n#### **Helper Function: `eval_variable` (Lines 12-43)**\n\n```cuda\n__device__ __forceinline__ FpExt\neval_variable(PackedVar var, uint32_t row, const EvalCoreCtx &ctx, uint32_t height) {\n    uint8_t entry_type = var.entry_type();\n    uint8_t offset = var.offset();\n    \n    switch (entry_type) {\n    case 1: { // MAIN\n        auto main_ptr = ctx.d_main[var.part_index()];\n        const auto stride = height * main_ptr.air_width;\n        const FpExt *__restrict__ matrix = main_ptr.data + stride * offset;\n        const FpExt *__restrict__ column = matrix + height * var.col_index();\n        return column[row];\n    }\n    case 0: { // PREPROCESSED\n        const auto stride = height * ctx.d_preprocessed.air_width;\n        const FpExt *__restrict__ matrix = ctx.d_preprocessed.data + stride * offset;\n        const FpExt *__restrict__ column = matrix + height * var.col_index();\n        return column[row];\n    }\n    case 3: // PUBLIC\n        return FpExt(ctx.d_public[var.col_index()]);\n    case 8: // IS_FIRST\n        return ctx.d_selectors[row];\n    case 9: // IS_LAST\n        return ctx.d_selectors[2 * height + row];\n    case 10: // IS_TRANSITION\n        return ctx.d_selectors[height + row];\n    }\n    return FpExt(Fp::zero());\n}\n```\n\n**Entry types mapping:**\n- 0: PREPROCESSED\n- 1: MAIN (needs part_index and offset)\n- 3: PUBLIC\n- 8: IS_FIRST (selector at `row`)\n- 9: IS_LAST (selector at `2*height + row`)\n- 10: IS_TRANSITION (selector at `height + row`)\n\n#### **Main Kernel: `zerocheck_monomial_kernel` (Lines 102-151)**\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void zerocheck_monomial_kernel(\n    FpExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums,      // Output: per-block sums\n    const BlockCtx *__restrict__ block_ctxs,\n    const MonomialAirCtx *__restrict__ air_ctxs,\n    uint32_t threads_per_block\n)\n```\n\n**Execution model:**\n- Grid: `(num_blocks, num_x)` where `blockIdx.x` = block index, `blockIdx.y` = x_int\n- Each block evaluates monomials for a specific (y_int, mono_block) pair\n- `blockCtx = block_ctxs[blockIdx.x]` has:\n  - `local_block_idx_x = y_int * mono_blocks + mono_block`\n  - `air_idx` = which AIR this block belongs to\n- Decoding (lines 114-123):\n  ```cuda\n  uint32_t num_x = gridDim.y;\n  uint32_t x_int = blockIdx.y;\n  uint32_t mono_blocks = (actx.num_monomials + threads_per_block - 1) / threads_per_block;\n  uint32_t y_int = bctx.local_block_idx_x / mono_blocks;\n  uint32_t mono_block = bctx.local_block_idx_x % mono_blocks;\n  uint32_t height = num_x * actx.num_y;\n  uint32_t row = x_int * actx.num_y + y_int;\n  ```\n\n**Computation (lines 127-150):**\n1. Each thread `threadIdx.x` evaluates one monomial: `m = mono_block * threads_per_block + threadIdx.x`\n2. For each monomial:\n   - Start with product = 1\n   - For each variable in the monomial: `product *= eval_variable(var, row, ...)`\n   - Multiply by precomputed `d_lambda_combinations[m]`\n   - Result stored in per-thread `sum`\n3. Block reduction via `sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(sum, shared)` - sums across all threads\n4. Thread 0 applies `eq_xi[y_int]` and stores to `tmp_sums[blockIdx.x * num_x + x_int]`\n\n**Shared memory:** `size_t shmem = div_ceil(block.x, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt)` (for warp reduction)\n\n#### **Launcher: `_zerocheck_monomial_batched` (Lines 153-192)**\n\n```cuda\nextern \"C\" int _zerocheck_monomial_batched(\n    FpExt *tmp_sums,\n    FpExt *output,\n    const BlockCtx *block_ctxs,\n    const MonomialAirCtx *air_ctxs,\n    const uint32_t *air_block_offsets,  // [num_airs+1]: segment start/end indices\n    uint32_t num_blocks,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t num_airs,\n    uint32_t threads_per_block\n)\n```\n\n**Two-phase execution:**\n1. **Phase 1** (line 173): Main kernel with grid `(num_blocks, num_x)`, block `(threads_per_block,)`\n2. **Phase 2** (line 187): Batched reduction kernel `sumcheck::batched_final_reduce_block_sums` with:\n   - Grid: `(num_airs, num_x)` - each block reduces one (AIR, x_int) pair\n   - Uses `air_block_offsets` to know which blocks belong to each AIR\n\n#### **Logup Monomial Kernel: `logup_monomial_kernel` (Lines 392-442)**\n\n```cuda\ntemplate <bool IS_DENOM>\n__global__ void logup_monomial_kernel(\n    FracExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums,    // FracExt = {p, q}\n    const BlockCtx *__restrict__ block_ctxs,\n    const LogupMonomialCommonCtx *__restrict__ common_ctxs,\n    const LogupMonomialCtx *__restrict__ ctxs\n)\n```\n\n**Key differences from zerocheck:**\n- Outputs `FracExt` (numerator and denominator) not `FpExt`\n- Two instances per AIR: numerator kernel (`IS_DENOM=false`) and denominator kernel (`IS_DENOM=true`)\n- Denominator kernel adds bus_term contribution: `reduced += bus_term_sum * eq_xi[y_int]` when `mono_block == 0`\n- For numerator: writes to `tmp_sums[...].p`\n- For denominator: writes to `tmp_sums[...].q`\n\n#### **Logup Launcher: `_logup_monomial_batched` (Lines 444-495)**\n\n```cuda\nextern \"C\" int _logup_monomial_batched(\n    FracExt *tmp_sums,\n    FracExt *output,\n    const BlockCtx *block_ctxs,\n    const LogupMonomialCommonCtx *common_ctxs,\n    const LogupMonomialCtx *numer_ctxs,\n    const LogupMonomialCtx *denom_ctxs,\n    const uint32_t *air_block_offsets,\n    uint32_t num_blocks,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t num_airs,\n    uint32_t threads_per_block\n)\n```\n\n**Three-phase execution:**\n1. Evaluate numerator monomials (line 465)\n2. Evaluate denominator monomials (line 473)\n3. Batched reduction (line 487): treats `FracExt` as 2x `FpExt`, so grid is `(num_airs, 2*num_x)`\n\n#### **Lambda Combination Precomputation (Lines 60-96)**\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void precompute_lambda_combinations_kernel(\n    FpExt *__restrict__ out,\n    const MonomialHeader *__restrict__ headers,\n    const LambdaTerm *__restrict__ lambda_terms,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ lambda_pows,\n    uint32_t num_monomials\n)\n```\n\nFor each monomial `m`:\n```\nsum = 0\nfor l in 0..hdr.num_terms:\n    term = lambda_terms[hdr.term_offset + l]\n    sum += lambda_pows[term.constraint_idx] * term.coefficient\nout[m] = sum\n```\n\n#### **Logup Combination Precomputation (Lines 303-364)**\n\nTwo kernels: numerator and denominator.\n\n**Numerator** (lines 329-345):\n```\nfor t in 0..hdr.num_terms:\n    term = terms[hdr.term_offset + t]\n    sum += eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx] * term.coefficient\nout[m] = sum\n```\n\n**Denominator** (lines 347-364, template `IS_DENOM=true`):\n```\nfor t in 0..hdr.num_terms:\n    term = terms[hdr.term_offset + t]\n    value = eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx] * term.coefficient * beta_pows[term.field_idx]\n    sum += value\nout[m] = sum\n```\n\n---\n\n### **2. RUST SIDE: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs`**\n\n#### **ZerocheckMonomialBatch Struct (Lines 111-217)**\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct ZerocheckMonomialBatch<'a> {\n    traces: Vec<&'a TraceCtx>,\n    block_ctxs: DeviceBuffer<BlockCtx>,\n    air_ctxs: DeviceBuffer<MonomialAirCtx>,\n    air_offsets: DeviceBuffer<u32>,\n}\n\nimpl<'a> ZerocheckMonomialBatch<'a> {\n    pub fn new<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n        traces: impl IntoIterator<Item = &'a TraceCtx>,\n        pk: &DeviceMultiStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n        lambda_combinations: &[&DeviceBuffer<EF>],\n    ) -> Result<Self, MemCopyError>\n```\n\n**Construction logic (lines 143-217):**\n1. For each trace, compute: `mono_blocks = ceil(num_monomials / THREADS_PER_BLOCK)`\n2. Total blocks per trace: `total_blocks = mono_blocks * num_y`\n3. For each local_idx in 0..total_blocks: create `BlockCtx` with:\n   - `local_block_idx_x = local_idx` (encodes both y_int and mono_block)\n   - `air_idx = local_air` (index within this batch)\n4. Build `air_offsets` array: `[0, trace0_total_blocks, trace0_total_blocks + trace1_total_blocks, ...]`\n5. Build `MonomialAirCtx` for each trace:\n   ```rust\n   MonomialAirCtx {\n       d_headers: monomials.d_headers.as_ptr(),\n       d_variables: monomials.d_variables.as_ptr(),\n       d_lambda_combinations: lc.as_ptr(),\n       num_monomials: monomials.num_monomials,\n       eval_ctx: EvalCoreCtx {\n           d_selectors: t.sels_ptr,\n           d_preprocessed: t.prep_ptr,\n           d_main: t.main_ptrs_dev.as_ptr(),\n           d_public: t.public_ptr,\n       },\n       d_eq_xi: t.eq_xi_ptr,\n       num_y: t.num_y,\n   }\n   ```\n\n**Evaluation (lines 229-266):**\n```rust\npub fn evaluate(&self, num_x: u32) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<EF>, KernelError> {\n    let num_blocks = self.block_ctxs.len();\n    let num_airs = self.air_ctxs.len();\n    \n    let mut tmp_sums = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(num_blocks * num_x as usize);\n    let mut output = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(num_airs * num_x as usize);\n    \n    unsafe {\n        zerocheck_monomial_batched(\n            &mut tmp_sums,\n            &mut output,\n            &self.block_ctxs,\n            &self.air_ctxs,\n            &self.air_offsets,\n            num_blocks as u32,\n            num_x,\n            num_airs as u32,\n            THREADS_PER_BLOCK,\n        )?;\n    }\n    Ok(output)\n}\n```\n\n**Output layout:** `[num_airs * num_x]` elements as `[air0_x0, air0_x1, ..., air1_x0, air1_x1, ...]`\n\n#### **ZerocheckMonomialParYBatch Struct (Lines 281-493)**\n\nVariant that parallelizes over y_int. Key differences:\n\n**Construction (lines 303-441):**\n- Uses smaller `THREADS_PER_BLOCK_PAR_Y = 128`\n- Auto-tunes `chunk_size` (monomials per thread) based on SM count\n- Block encoding: `local_block_idx_x = y_block * air_mono_chunks + mono_chunk`\n- Each thread loops over `chunk_size` consecutive monomials\n\n**Kernel differences (batch_mle_monomial.cu lines 198-256):**\n```cuda\n// Each thread handles one y_int and loops over a chunk of monomials\nuint32_t y_int = threadIdx.x + y_block * threads_per_block;\nbool active = (y_int < actx.num_y);\nuint32_t mono_start = mono_chunk * chunk_size;\nuint32_t mono_end = min(mono_start + chunk_size, actx.num_monomials);\n\nFpExt sum(Fp::zero());\nif (active) {\n    for (uint32_t m = mono_start; m < mono_end; ++m) {\n        // Evaluate monomial m\n        sum += product * actx.d_lambda_combinations[m];\n    }\n    sum *= actx.d_eq_xi[y_int];\n}\n\nFpExt reduced = sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(sum, shared);\nif (threadIdx.x == 0) {\n    tmp_sums[blockIdx.x * num_x + x_int] = reduced;\n}\n```\n\n#### **LogupMonomialBatch Struct (Lines 588-793)**\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct LogupMonomialBatch<'a> {\n    traces: Vec<&'a TraceCtx>,\n    block_ctxs: DeviceBuffer<BlockCtx>,\n    common_ctxs: DeviceBuffer<LogupMonomialCommonCtx>,\n    numer_ctxs: DeviceBuffer<LogupMonomialCtx>,\n    denom_ctxs: DeviceBuffer<LogupMonomialCtx>,\n    air_offsets: DeviceBuffer<u32>,\n    num_blocks: u32,\n}\n```\n\n**Construction (lines 607-741):**\n1. For each trace: `max_monomials = max(num_numer, num_denom)`\n2. `mono_blocks = ceil(max_monomials / THREADS_PER_BLOCK_LOGUP)`\n3. Create blocks for all (y_int, mono_block) pairs: `y_int * mono_blocks + mono_block`\n4. Build three context vectors:\n   - `common_ctxs`: one per trace (eval_ctx, eq_xi, bus_term_sum, num_y, mono_blocks)\n   - `numer_ctxs`: one per trace (numerator monomial headers/variables/combinations)\n   - `denom_ctxs`: one per trace (denominator monomial headers/variables/combinations)\n\n**Evaluation (lines 753-792):**\n```rust\npub fn evaluate(&self, num_x: u32) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, KernelError> {\n    let num_airs = self.common_ctxs.len();\n    \n    let mut tmp_sums = DeviceBuffer::<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(\n        self.num_blocks as usize * num_x as usize\n    );\n    let mut output = DeviceBuffer::<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(num_airs * num_x as usize);\n    \n    unsafe {\n        logup_monomial_batched(\n            &mut tmp_sums,\n            &mut output,\n            &self.block_ctxs,\n            &self.common_ctxs,\n            &self.numer_ctxs,\n            &self.denom_ctxs,\n            &self.air_offsets,\n            self.num_blocks,\n            num_x,\n            num_airs as u32,\n            THREADS_PER_BLOCK_LOGUP,\n        )?;\n    }\n    Ok(output)\n}\n```\n\n**Output layout:** `[num_airs * num_x]` FracExt elements\n\n#### **LogupCombinations Precomputation (Lines 500-580)**\n\n```rust\npub struct LogupCombinations {\n    pub d_numer_combinations: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    pub d_denom_combinations: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    pub bus_term_sum: EF,\n}\n\npub(crate) fn compute_logup_combinations<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceMultiStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    air_idx: usize,\n    d_beta_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    d_eq_3bs: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    eq_3bs_host: &[EF],\n    beta_pows_host: &[EF],\n) -> Result<LogupCombinations, CudaError>\n```\n\nComputes `bus_term_sum` on CPU (lines 561-573):\n```rust\nlet interactions = &pk.per_air[air_idx].vk.symbolic_constraints.interactions;\nlet mut bus_term_sum = EF::ZERO;\nfor (i, interaction) in interactions.iter().enumerate() {\n    let beta_len = beta_pows_host[interaction.message.len()];\n    let bus_idx = interaction.bus_index as u32;\n    bus_term_sum += beta_len * EF::from_u32(bus_idx + 1) * eq_3bs_host[i];\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. FFI BINDING FILE: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`**\n\n#### **Key C Structs (Lines 8-96)**\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct BlockCtx {\n    pub local_block_idx_x: u32,\n    pub air_idx: u32,\n}\n\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct MonomialAirCtx {\n    pub d_headers: *const MonomialHeader,\n    pub d_variables: *const PackedVar,\n    pub d_lambda_combinations: *const EF,\n    pub num_monomials: u32,\n    pub eval_ctx: EvalCoreCtx,\n    pub d_eq_xi: *const EF,\n    pub num_y: u32,\n}\n\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct EvalCoreCtx {\n    pub d_selectors: *const EF,\n    pub d_preprocessed: MainMatrixPtrs<EF>,\n    pub d_main: *const MainMatrixPtrs<EF>,\n    pub d_public: *const F,\n}\n\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct MainMatrixPtrs<T> {\n    pub data: *const T,\n    pub air_width: u32,\n}\n\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct LogupMonomialCommonCtx {\n    pub eval_ctx: EvalCoreCtx,\n    pub d_eq_xi: *const EF,\n    pub bus_term_sum: EF,\n    pub num_y: u32,\n    pub mono_blocks: u32,\n}\n\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct LogupMonomialCtx {\n    pub d_headers: *const MonomialHeader,\n    pub d_variables: *const PackedVar,\n    pub d_combinations: *const EF,\n    pub num_monomials: u32,\n}\n```\n\n#### **FFI Function Signatures (Lines 527-590)**\n\n```rust\nextern \"C\" {\n    fn _zerocheck_monomial_batched(\n        tmp_sums: *mut EF,\n        output: *mut EF,\n        block_ctxs: *const BlockCtx,\n        air_ctxs: *const MonomialAirCtx,\n        air_block_offsets: *const u32,\n        num_blocks: u32,\n        num_x: u32,\n        num_airs: u32,\n        threads_per_block: u32,\n    ) -> i32;\n\n    fn _zerocheck_monomial_par_y_batched(\n        tmp_sums: *mut EF,\n        output: *mut EF,\n        block_ctxs: *const BlockCtx,\n        air_ctxs: *const MonomialAirCtx,\n        air_block_offsets: *const u32,\n        num_blocks: u32,\n        num_x: u32,\n        num_airs: u32,\n        chunk_size: u32,\n        threads_per_block: u32,\n    ) -> i32;\n\n    fn _precompute_lambda_combinations(\n        out: *mut EF,\n        headers: *const MonomialHeader,\n        lambda_terms: *const LambdaTerm<F>,\n        lambda_pows: *const EF,\n        num_monomials: u32,\n    ) -> i32;\n\n    fn _precompute_logup_numer_combinations(\n        out: *mut EF,\n        headers: *const MonomialHeader,\n        terms: *const InteractionMonomialTerm<F>,\n        eq_3bs: *const EF,\n        num_monomials: u32,\n    ) -> i32;\n\n    fn _precompute_logup_denom_combinations(\n        out: *mut EF,\n        headers: *const MonomialHeader,\n        terms: *const InteractionMonomialTerm<F>,\n        beta_pows: *const EF,\n        eq_3bs: *const EF,\n        num_monomials: u32,\n    ) -> i32;\n\n    fn _logup_monomial_batched(\n        tmp_sums: *mut Frac<EF>,\n        output: *mut Frac<EF>,\n        block_ctxs: *const BlockCtx,\n        common_ctxs: *const LogupMonomialCommonCtx,\n        numer_ctxs: *const LogupMonomialCtx,\n        denom_ctxs: *const LogupMonomialCtx,\n        air_block_offsets: *const u32,\n        num_blocks: u32,\n        num_x: u32,\n        num_airs: u32,\n        threads_per_block: u32,\n    ) -> i32;\n}\n```\n\n#### **Rust Wrapper Functions (Lines 1266-1394)**\n\nAll call corresponding `_` prefixed C functions with proper type conversions.\n\n---\n\n### **4. SUPPORTING HEADER FILES**\n\n#### **monomial.cuh** (`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/include/monomial.cuh`)\n\n```cuda\nstruct PackedVar {\n    uint32_t data;\n    // Bits 0-3:   entry_type\n    // Bits 4-11:  part_index\n    // Bits 12-15: offset\n    // Bits 16-31: col_index\n    __device__ __forceinline__ uint8_t entry_type() const { return data & 0xF; }\n    __device__ __forceinline__ uint8_t part_index() const { return (data >> 4) & 0xFF; }\n    __device__ __forceinline__ uint8_t offset() const { return (data >> 12) & 0xF; }\n    __device__ __forceinline__ uint16_t col_index() const { return data >> 16; }\n};\n\nstruct MonomialHeader {\n    uint32_t var_offset;\n    uint32_t term_offset;\n    uint16_t num_vars;\n    uint16_t num_terms;\n};\n\nstruct LambdaTerm {\n    uint32_t constraint_idx;\n    Fp coefficient;\n};\n\nstruct InteractionMonomialTerm {\n    Fp coefficient;\n    uint16_t interaction_idx;\n    uint16_t field_idx;\n};\n```\n\n#### **sumcheck.cuh** - Block Reduction\n\n```cuda\nstatic __device__ inline FpExt block_reduce_sum(FpExt val, FpExt *shared) {\n    // Two-stage: warp reduces, then first warp reduces per-warp results\n    // Lane 0 of each warp writes to shared[warp_id]\n    // Returns reduced value (valid in all threads of first warp)\n}\n\nstatic __global__ void batched_final_reduce_block_sums(\n    const FpExt *block_sums,           // [total_blocks][d]\n    FpExt *output,                     // [num_segments][d]\n    const uint32_t *segment_offsets,   // [num_segments + 1]\n    uint32_t d\n) {\n    // Grid: (num_segments, d)\n    // Each block (seg_idx, out_idx) reduces its segment's blocks\n    uint32_t start = segment_offsets[seg_idx];\n    uint32_t end = segment_offsets[seg_idx + 1];\n    uint32_t num_blocks = end - start;\n    // Each thread accumulates strided subset, block reduces, thread 0 writes output\n}\n```\n\n#### **eval_ctx.cuh** - GPU-side EvalCoreCtx\n\n```cuda\nstruct EvalCoreCtx {\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_selectors;\n    const MainMatrixPtrs<FpExt> d_preprocessed;\n    const MainMatrixPtrs<FpExt> *__restrict__ d_main;\n    const Fp *__restrict__ d_public;\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### **5. KEY CONSTANTS & COMPILATION PARAMETERS**\n\nFrom `batch_mle_monomial.rs`:\n- `THREADS_PER_BLOCK = 256` (zerocheck)\n- `THREADS_PER_BLOCK_PAR_Y = 128` (par-y variant)\n- `THREADS_PER_BLOCK_LOGUP = 128` (logup)\n- `WARP_SIZE = 32` (from launcher.cuh)\n\nShared memory per block:\n- `shmem = div_ceil(threads_per_block, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt)` = number of warps × 16 bytes\n\n---\n\n### **6. EXECUTION DATA FLOW SUMMARY**\n\n**Zerocheck Monomial Flow:**\n1. `compute_lambda_combinations()` → precomputes `d_lambda_combinations` for each AIR\n2. `ZerocheckMonomialBatch::new()` → builds block/air contexts\n3. `ZerocheckMonomialBatch::evaluate(num_x)` → calls `zerocheck_monomial_batched()`\n4. Kernel Phase 1: `zerocheck_monomial_kernel` evaluates all (y_int, mono_block) pairs, produces `tmp_sums[num_blocks * num_x]`\n5. Kernel Phase 2: `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` reduces per-AIR blocks, outputs `[num_airs * num_x]`\n\n**Logup Monomial Flow:**\n1. `compute_logup_combinations()` → precomputes numerator/denominator combinations + bus_term_sum\n2. `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` → builds all three context types\n3. `LogupMonomialBatch::evaluate(num_x)` → calls `logup_monomial_batched()`\n4. Kernel Phase 1a: `logup_monomial_kernel<false>` evaluates numerator monomials\n5. Kernel Phase 1b: `logup_monomial_kernel<true>` evaluates denominator monomials (adds bus_term)\n6. Kernel Phase 2: Reduction as FpExt (2×num_x per reduction), outputs `[num_airs * num_x]` FracExt\n\n---\n\nThis implementation enables efficient batch evaluation of multiple traces' monomials in a single GPU kernel launch, with two scheduling strategies (monomial-parallel and y-parallel)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"997f7e33-9a1a-40a3-8498-75cdc1cf5ede","uuid":"dfc8ce1d-b92e-43c9-b18c-dbcca0e1c4ce","timestamp":"2026-04-14T21:25:31.299Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the current implementation of the zerocheck monomial and logup monomial kernels in the CUDA backend. Read the following files thoroughly and report their structure, key functions, and relevant details:\n\n1. `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu` - The CUDA kernel file. Focus on:\n   - The `zerocheck_monomial_kernel` (around line 102-151)\n   - The `logup_monomial_kernel` \n   - The `warp_reduce_sum` function\n   - The C launcher functions (`_zerocheck_monomial_batched`, `_logup_monomial_batched`)\n   - The `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` kernel\n   - The `MonomialAirCtx` struct\n   - Available helper functions like `eval_variable`\n\n2. `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs` - The Rust side. Focus on:\n   - `ZerocheckMonomialBatch` struct and its `new()` and `evaluate()` methods\n   - `LogupMonomialBatch` struct and its `new()` and `evaluate()` methods\n   - How traces are stored and indexed\n   - The FFI bindings (extern \"C\" functions)\n   - The `MonomialAirCtx` struct on Rust side\n   - The `BlockCtx` struct\n   - How output is consumed by callers\n\n3. `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` - The FFI binding file for the CUDA functions.\n\nReport the full content of key structs, function signatures, and enough surrounding code that I can implement new kernels correctly. Be very thorough - I need line numbers, struct layouts, parameter types, and how the existing code routes traces to kernels.","agentId":"aeb7a175539c52a43","agentType":"