ace `seg_idx`, where `seg_idx` ranges from 0 to num_block_traces. But then `BlockCtx.air_idx` needs to be block-local (0, 1, 2, ...) to match the reduction kernel's `seg_idx`, which means `air_ctxs` should have block-trace contexts at those positions instead of the original global indices.\n\nActually, I think the cleanest approach is to maintain two separate arrays: one with all traces in original order for the warp kernel, and another with just the block-eligible traces in block-local order for the block kernel.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4902,"cache_read_input_tokens":120352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4902},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"997f7e33-9a1a-40a3-8498-75cdc1cf5ede","uuid":"535275af-6ea1-4183-bd4c-54b2b8437fca"}
